#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Feature Test Macro Requirements for glibc (see B<feature_test_macros>(7)):"
msgstr ""
"Requisitos de Macros de Prueba de Características para glibc (véase "
"B<feature_test_macros>(7)):"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "B<nan>(), B<nanf>(), B<nanl>():"
msgstr "B<nan>(), B<nanf>(), B<nanl>():"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    _ISOC99_SOURCE || _POSIX_C_SOURCE E<gt>= 200112L\n"
msgstr "    _ISOC99_SOURCE || _POSIX_C_SOURCE E<gt>= 200112L\n"

#. type: SH
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "DESCRIPCIÓN"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"These functions return a representation (determined by I<tagp>)  of a quiet "
"NaN.  If the implementation does not support quiet NaNs, these functions "
"return zero."
msgstr ""
"Estas funciones devuelven una representación (determinada por I<tagp>)  de "
"un NaN privado. Si la implementación no soporta NaNs privados, estas "
"funciones devuelven cero."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The call I<nan(\"char-sequence\")> is equivalent to:"
msgstr "La llamada I<nan(\"secuencia-de-caracteres\")> es equivalente a:"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "strtod(\"NAN(char-sequence)\", NULL);\n"
msgstr "strtod(\"NAN(secuencia-de-caracteres)\", NULL);\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Similarly, calls to B<nanf>()  and B<nanl>()  are equivalent to analogous "
"calls to B<strtof>(3)  and B<strtold>(3)."
msgstr ""
"Similarmente las llamadas B<nanf>() y B<nanl>() son equivalentes a las "
"llamadas análogas B<strtof>(3) y B<strtold>(3)."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The argument I<tagp> is used in an unspecified manner.  On IEEE 754 systems, "
"there are many representations of NaN, and I<tagp> selects one.  On other "
"systems it may do nothing."
msgstr ""
"El argumento I<tagp> se utiliza de manera indefinida. En sistemas IEEE 754, "
"hay muchas representaciones de NaN y I<tagp> escoge una. En otros sistemas "
"puede que no haga nada."

